Author: María <mariagrandury@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 01:09:15 2026 +0200

    evals: probe group with cloze BBH/ACP, INCLUDE v2 and probe rf twins
    
    A screening pass over candidate benchmarks at each cell's last checkpoint,
    kept out of `auto` so the watchers never top up every checkpoint with it:
    `auto_evals_cscs.py --group NAME --final-only`, jobs suffixed by the
    group name. `groups.auto_probe` holds 19 benchmarks, `auto_include_v2`
    the 154 INCLUDE v2 tasks (L50, OG + EN).
    
    BBH and ACP-Bench are mixed families, so `make_cloze_tasks.py` splits them
    by what the data says each subtask is and registers one benchmark per
    arm: bbh_mcq / rf_bbh_mcq (17, the reformulation pair), bbh_cloze (6
    two-way, no twin), and the same three for acp_bench (7 each). The four
    free-form BBH subtasks are not written. n_options is the item-weighted
    effective count and n_items the surviving count, both from the data.
    
    The probe twins from `make_rf_tasks.py` (mmlu, commonsense_qa,
    cultural_bench_easy) `include:` the original YAML by absolute path:
    copying keys turned process_docs into a string and dropped
    commonsense_qa's validation split. cultural_bench_hard is 2-way and
    already cloze, so it has no twin and its chance level is 1/2.
    INCLUDE v2 reads the cached parquet directly; hub resolution picked a
    revision with no prepared cache and all 154 tasks died offline.
    
    `utils.configs.write_tasks_json` refuses to write over a tasks.json that
    changed underneath: two generators overlapping silently lost 154
    registrations once.
    
    Verified: 147 tasks loaded through a real TaskManager (gold in range,
    declared n_options = scored, n_items exact); twin row counts match the
    originals bar one blank row; all three generators byte-idempotent;
    dry runs price 84 + 77 jobs, ~86 node-h, all suffixed.
    
    Also: .gitignore core_clariden* (a 944 MB core dump sat untracked).

